  <compounddef id="dde" kind="page">
    <compoundname>dde</compoundname>
    <title>Adding Delays</title>
    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><anchor id="dde_1md_src_2examples_2dde"/></para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>This page assumes familiarity with the basic layout and API usage described in the main <ref refid="examples" kindref="compound">Examples</ref> page.</para>
</simplesect>
Delay differential equations (DDEs) are characterised by delayed (historical) states influencing the current state of an agent, written as</para>
<para><formula id="50">\[    \frac{d\vec{Y}}{dt} = \vec{F}(\vec{Y}(t),~\vec{Y}(t-\vec{\tau}_1),~\vec{Y}(t-\vec{\tau}_2),~\dots~\vec{Y}(t-\vec{\tau}_n),~t),
\]</formula></para>
<para>where the <formula id="51">$\tau_i$</formula> are the delay terms. Since ODE systems are only defined for <formula id="52">$t\ge t_0$</formula> (with <formula id="53">$t_0=0$</formula> in NDXL), one inevitably encounters the situation where <formula id="54">$t-\tau&lt;t_0$</formula>. This is solved by use of a history function, which is a special function in DDEs defined for the interval <formula id="55">$t_0-\tau$</formula> that returns the historical states over that time period i.e., &quot;what was the system doing before we started modelling/tracking it?&quot;</para>
<para>In NDXL, delays have a physical interpretation as being the time taken for information to travel from vertex <formula id="20">$i$</formula> to <formula id="42">$j$</formula> along edge <formula id="22">$ij$</formula> i.e., the stage state is only delayed because the edge propagates that information at a finite speed. This interpretation has several important implications:</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Delays are a property of an edge, with idealised instantaneous information transfer occuring only along edges whose delay is zero</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Information has not yet propagated between vertices <formula id="20">$i$</formula> and <formula id="42">$j$</formula> along edge <formula id="22">$ij$</formula> for <formula id="56">$t&lt;\tau_{ij}$</formula></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Historical states for vertices <formula id="20">$i$</formula> and <formula id="42">$j$</formula> need only be stored up to <formula id="57">$t-\tau_{ij}$</formula></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>The first inference means that only vertex dynamics, never edge dynamics, can be described by DDEs in NDXL, and vertex <formula id="20">$i$</formula> can only ever depend on the delayed state of vertex <formula id="42">$j$</formula>; for vertex <formula id="20">$i$</formula> to depend on its own delayed state, vertex <formula id="20">$i$</formula> and vertex <formula id="42">$j$</formula> must be the same vertex i.e., a self-coupled node. For vertex <formula id="20">$i$</formula> to be affected by multiple delayed terms from vertex <formula id="42">$j$</formula>, mutliple edges <formula id="22">$ij$</formula> must exist, each with its own unique delay. The second inference implies that the history function for vertices is <formula id="58">$\vec{x}_0$</formula>, and for edges is <formula id="59">$\vec{0}$</formula>, for <formula id="60">$t&lt;\tau$</formula>; this is what the functions <ref refid="group__vertex__getters_1gad7f8cbc780425384693f7e4163f51ed7" kindref="member">ndxlGetVertexNeighbourState()</ref> <ref refid="group__edge__getters_1ga9d08c32c646317343fb9e99b78e204eb" kindref="member">ndxlGetEdgeRelativeState()</ref> do, and is why they should almost always be used over retrieving agent states directly. The third inference is more of a concern for memory management, where an indefinite number of historical states cannot be stored on a finite amount of memory, meaning NDXL only preserves historical states up to <formula id="57">$t-\tau_{ij}$</formula>. Historical states are further used to perform a cubic hermite interpolation when <formula id="57">$t-\tau_{ij}$</formula> does not correspond directly to a discrete stored state (we opted for cubic hermite interpolation due to its curvature preservation properties).</para>
<sect1 id="dde_1ovm">
<title>Optimal Velocity Model</title><para>We consider a delayed optimal velocity model (OVM) with <formula id="61">$20$</formula> cars travelling in a circle, where the position <formula id="62">$x$</formula> and velocity <formula id="63">$v$</formula> of car <formula id="20">$i$</formula> are given by the already-deconstructed second-order ODE</para>
<para><formula id="64">\[    \frac{dx_i}{dt} = v_i,
\]</formula>   <formula id="65">\[    \frac{dv_i}{dt} = a_i\left[V\left(\Delta x_i(t-\tau_{ii})\right) - v_i\right].
\]</formula></para>
<para>The delays here refer to the drivers&apos; reaction times, and the optimal velocity function <formula id="66">$V$</formula> typically takes on a sigmoid curve such as</para>
<para><formula id="67">\[    V\left(\Delta x\right) = v_{max}\frac{\tanh{(\Delta x - d)} + \tanh{(d)}}{1 + \tanh{(d)}},
\]</formula></para>
<para>where <formula id="68">$\Delta x(t-\tau_{ij})$</formula> is the distance between cars <formula id="20">$i$</formula> and <formula id="42">$j$</formula>, <formula id="69">$\tau_{ij}$</formula> time ago.</para>
<para>We see that each car (vertex) depends on a delayed state from the car in front of it, and of itself. Furthermore, each car is not influenced by the car behind it; our network therefore consists of vertices each with a directed edge to the vertex &quot;behind&quot; it, and a directed edge to itself (it is usually a good idea to make self-loops directed to avoid duplicate state storage and wasted memory). We define the car dynamics function with this structure in mind, remembering also that the order in which edges are added is preserved. In our dynamics function, we therefore query each edge for its neighbouring vertex, and query the network for common parameters like <formula id="70">$v_{max}$</formula>.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".c"><codeline><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>...</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>We<sp/>again<sp/>use<sp/>a<sp/>custom<sp/>struct<sp/>to<sp/>combine<sp/>numerical<sp/>network<sp/>parameters<sp/>with<sp/>a<sp/>file<sp/>handle</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">typedef</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">struct</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>vmax;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>d;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>tanhd;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>FILE*<sp/>handle;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}<sp/>nwkparams;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>acc(<ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1ad03a49b11a22416ba63273c4d7deb38b" kindref="member">NDXLVertex</ref>*<sp/>car,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal">*<sp/>dxv_i,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">const</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal">*<sp/>xv_i,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>t,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">void</highlight><highlight class="normal">*<sp/>p)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>vmax<sp/>=<sp/>(*(nwkparams*)<ref refid="group__network__getters_1ga995644f99e39725649115b8080f5f486" kindref="member">ndxlGetNetworkParams</ref>(<ref refid="group__vertex__getters_1ga92fbd8f6bb5ad59c012826f2205226c3" kindref="member">ndxlGetVertexNetwork</ref>(car))).vmax;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>d<sp/>=<sp/>(*(nwkparams*)<ref refid="group__network__getters_1ga995644f99e39725649115b8080f5f486" kindref="member">ndxlGetNetworkParams</ref>(<ref refid="group__vertex__getters_1ga92fbd8f6bb5ad59c012826f2205226c3" kindref="member">ndxlGetVertexNetwork</ref>(car))).d;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>tanhd<sp/>=<sp/>(*(nwkparams*)<ref refid="group__network__getters_1ga995644f99e39725649115b8080f5f486" kindref="member">ndxlGetNetworkParams</ref>(<ref refid="group__vertex__getters_1ga92fbd8f6bb5ad59c012826f2205226c3" kindref="member">ndxlGetVertexNetwork</ref>(car))).tanhd;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>a<sp/>=<sp/>*(</highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal">*)p;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>x_ahead,<sp/>x_delayed;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Since<sp/>each<sp/>vertex<sp/>has<sp/>three<sp/>edges<sp/>(one<sp/>incoming,<sp/>one<sp/>outgoing,<sp/>and<sp/>one<sp/>self-loop),<sp/>we<sp/>iterate<sp/>over<sp/>all<sp/>three<sp/>to<sp/>appropriately<sp/>populate<sp/>x_ahead<sp/>and<sp/>x_delayed</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">for</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(<ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1aa30ac2f40da4dbe7d841088a78f957fe" kindref="member">NDXLEdge</ref>*<sp/>edge<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="group__vertex__traversal_1ga37847adf2ab313359a11a28196cfa565" kindref="member">ndxlGetVertexFirstEdge</ref>(car);<sp/>edge;<sp/>edge<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="group__vertex__traversal_1gac1816923b2d91d36fd628ef8fdb36e02" kindref="member">ndxlGetVertexNextEdge</ref>(car,<sp/>edge))</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Check<sp/>for<sp/>self-loop</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">if</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(<ref refid="group__vertex__getters_1ga17c6a47ca779d2e1cd63d3560a25a6d2" kindref="member">ndxlGetVertexNeighbour</ref>(car,<sp/>edge)<sp/>==<sp/>car)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Because<sp/>the<sp/>equations<sp/>are<sp/>delayed,<sp/>we<sp/>must<sp/>use<sp/>ndxlGetVertexNeighbourState()<sp/>to<sp/>factor<sp/>in<sp/>those<sp/>delays</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>This<sp/>is<sp/>even<sp/>true<sp/>for<sp/>the<sp/>self-loop,<sp/>as<sp/>the<sp/>historical<sp/>state<sp/>information<sp/>for<sp/>the<sp/>&quot;neighbour&quot;<sp/>is<sp/>what<sp/>we<sp/>want<sp/>to<sp/>query<sp/>(just<sp/>that<sp/>the<sp/>&quot;neighbour&quot;<sp/>happens<sp/>to<sp/>be<sp/>the<sp/>vertex<sp/>itself)</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>x_delayed<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="group__vertex__getters_1gad7f8cbc780425384693f7e4163f51ed7" kindref="member">ndxlGetVertexNeighbourState</ref>(car,<sp/>edge)[0];</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Check<sp/>for<sp/>`car`<sp/>being<sp/>the<sp/>&quot;destination&quot;<sp/>vertex<sp/>along<sp/>`edge`<sp/>i.e.,<sp/>information<sp/>flows<sp/>&quot;to&quot;<sp/>`car`</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">else</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">if</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(car<sp/>==<sp/><ref refid="group__edge__getters_1ga1cd64a902c4702ed87388ba9e4449fb7" kindref="member">ndxlGetEdgeSecondVertex</ref>(edge))</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>x_ahead<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="group__vertex__getters_1gad7f8cbc780425384693f7e4163f51ed7" kindref="member">ndxlGetVertexNeighbourState</ref>(car,<sp/>edge)[0];</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Calculate<sp/>optimal<sp/>velocity<sp/>and<sp/>write<sp/>out<sp/>derivatives</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>V<sp/>=<sp/>vmax<sp/>*<sp/>(tanh(x_ahead<sp/>-<sp/>x_delayed<sp/>-<sp/>d)<sp/>+<sp/>tanhd)<sp/>/<sp/>(1.0<sp/>+<sp/>tanhd);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>dxv_i[0]<sp/>=<sp/>xv_i[1];</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>dxv_i[1]<sp/>=<sp/>a<sp/>*<sp/>(V<sp/>-<sp/>xv_i[1]);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">return</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>0;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>Over in <computeroutput>main()</computeroutput>, we will create our cars and the edges between them, baring in mind that <computeroutput>directed</computeroutput> edges allow information to travel from its source vertex to its destination vertex, but not the other way around. The order in which we specify the vertices in the <ref refid="group__edge__creation_1ga64a610b6a899977bbf5722ca30f92114" kindref="member">edge constructor</ref> therefore becomes important, although their states can still be left as <computeroutput>NULL</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".c"><codeline><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>...</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>main(</highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>argc,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">char</highlight><highlight class="normal">**<sp/>argv)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><ref refid="group__lib__mgmt_1gaf795d2bbc114d928901bc9700830df4e" kindref="member">ndxlInit</ref>();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Define<sp/>network-wide<sp/>parameters<sp/>and<sp/>create<sp/>network</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>nwkparams<sp/>p;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>p.vmax<sp/>=<sp/>60.<sp/>*<sp/>(1000.<sp/>/<sp/>3600.);<sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Speed<sp/>limit<sp/>of<sp/>60<sp/>kph<sp/>in<sp/>m/s</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>p.d<sp/>=<sp/>1.5;<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Safe<sp/>bumber-to-bumber<sp/>distance<sp/>in<sp/>m</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>p.tanhd<sp/>=<sp/>tanh(p.d);<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Precalculate<sp/>tanh(d)<sp/>to<sp/>save<sp/>time<sp/>in<sp/>function<sp/>evaluations</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Prepare<sp/>output<sp/>file<sp/>and<sp/>create<sp/>network</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>p.handle<sp/>=<sp/>fopen(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;cars.csv&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;w&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">if</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(!p.handle)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">return</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>1;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>fprintf(p.handle,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;t&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><ref refid="group__ndxl__objects_1gaefd105209efdd9f61bea4c3f76770d37" kindref="member">NDXLNetwork</ref>*<sp/>nwk<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="group__network__creation_1gaceb794444113eebd20d8a6fabdc2e2f9" kindref="member">ndxlCreateNetwork</ref>(&amp;p);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Create<sp/>car<sp/>vertices,<sp/>recalling<sp/>that<sp/>their<sp/>`void*<sp/>params`<sp/>pointers<sp/>must<sp/>persist<sp/>in<sp/>memory</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>a[20];<sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Reaction<sp/>sensitivity</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>tau[20];<sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Reaction<sp/>time<sp/>(will<sp/>be<sp/>used<sp/>in<sp/>edge<sp/>creation<sp/>so<sp/>we<sp/>need<sp/>to<sp/>populate<sp/>them<sp/>now)</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1ad03a49b11a22416ba63273c4d7deb38b" kindref="member">NDXLVertex</ref>*<sp/>cars[20];</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">for</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>i<sp/>=<sp/>0;<sp/>i<sp/>&lt;<sp/>20;<sp/>i++)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Cars<sp/>start<sp/>uniformly<sp/>spaced<sp/>around<sp/>a<sp/>circle<sp/>of<sp/>circumference<sp/>100</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>xv0[2]<sp/>=<sp/>{<sp/>5.0<sp/>*<sp/>i,<sp/>randdbl(10.0,<sp/>15.0)<sp/>};</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>a[i]<sp/>=<sp/>randdbl(0.1,<sp/>0.3);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>tau[i]<sp/>=<sp/>randdbl(0.5,<sp/>1.5);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>cars[i]<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="group__vertex__creation_1gaec4b6881830464281fc35817e96bfaf3" kindref="member">ndxlCreateVertex</ref>(nwk,<sp/>xv0,<sp/>2,<sp/>acc,<sp/>NULL,<sp/>NULL,<sp/>0,<sp/>NULL,<sp/>&amp;a[i]);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Write<sp/>header<sp/>to<sp/>csv</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>fprintf(p.handle,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;,x%d&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>i);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>fprintf(p.handle,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;\n&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Create<sp/>edges<sp/>according<sp/>to<sp/>the<sp/>topology<sp/>described<sp/>above</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">for</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>i<sp/>=<sp/>0;<sp/>i<sp/>&lt;<sp/>20;<sp/>i++)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
