<para>Since the governing equation is fundamentally second-order, we will use the <ref refid="group__network__simulation_1gafb26d16d894bd6dc45fdd7b69c6c06f8" kindref="member">static Nystr<oumlaut/>m method</ref> to simulate the network, as it is better suited than the <ref refid="group__network__simulation_1ga86f19459b1504a9cc772383d5adc6556" kindref="member">static Ralston method</ref> to second-order equations. Outputs are plotted on a circle with circumference <formula id="71">$100$</formula> as that ringlike structure is how we defined our network in the first place.</para>
